    "result_text": "The full test suite (one test class, `AcceptanceTest`) is green and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans \u2014 while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`mapper/TelephoneDisplay.java`** (new) \u2014 a static helper, following the same convention as the sibling derived-field helpers (`LuhnCheckDigit`, `AgeBand`, `OwnerLocality`). `forE164` splits off the country code (longest-prefix match against known calling codes `+61`/`+1`, falling back to a single-digit code) and groups the national digits in threes from the left, joined to the country code by a single space: `\"+61412345678\"` \u2192 `\"+61 412 345 678\"`.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `telephoneDisplay` deriving it from `owner.getTelephone()`, alongside the other derived read-only fields.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated by the openapi-generator plugin, so the setter the mapper calls is produced from this).\n\nThe test feeds `telephone: \"0412 345 678\"`, which the existing `TelephoneNormalizer` canonicalizes to `+61412345678` (stored/returned as raw `telephone`), and the response now also returns `telephoneDisplay: \"+61 412 345 678\"`.",
